# Frontend API Integration – Full Implementation Plan

## Background

The backend is a Laravel API (`/api/v1/*`) with full CRUD for: **Clients**, **Employees**, **Tasks**, **Transactions**. The frontend is a React + Vite + TailwindCSS v4 app using TanStack Query v5 and React Hook Form.

**Discovery summary:**
- ✅ `src/api/axios.js` — Centralized Axios instance with Bearer token interceptor and `auth:logout` event dispatch.
- ✅ `src/hooks/api/` — All five hooks exist (`useAuth`, `useClients`, `useEmployees`, `useTasks`, `useTransactions`) with full CRUD + `invalidateQueries` on every mutation. **No new hooks needed.**
- ❌ Dashboard list pages (`Clients`, `Employees`, `Tasks`, `Transactions`) — Use **hardcoded mock data**. Must be wired to real API.
- ❌ Form pages (`ClientForm`, `EmployeeForm`, `TaskForm`, `TransactionForm`) — Form logic works but `onSubmit` only `console.log`s. Must call `useMutation`.
- ❌ Details pages (`ClientDetails`, `EmployeeDetails`, `TaskDetails`, `TransactionDetails`) — Use hardcoded data / broken imports (`useClients` called as `mutateAsync`). Must call `useQuery`.
- ✅ Routing — All routes are already registered in `AppRoutes.jsx`. No new routes needed.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The existing hooks accept **no filter params** (e.g., `?search=...&status=...`). I will upgrade them to accept a `filters` object that gets forwarded to the API as query params. This is a non-breaking extension.

> [!WARNING]
> `ClientDetails.jsx` line 10 has a critical bug: `useClients(id)` is called as `mutateAsync` — this crashes on render. My fix replaces it with the correct `useClient(id)` query hook.

> [!WARNING]
> `EmployeeDetails.jsx` has no API call at all — it renders 100% hardcoded data. My fix wires it to `useEmployee(id)`.

> [!NOTE]
> The `TaskForm` needs to fetch **clients** and **employees** from the API for its dropdowns — the original code has `// todo api` comments for this. I will fulfill this using the existing `useClients` and `useEmployees` hooks.

> [!NOTE]
> The `TransactionForm` needs clients, employees, and tasks for conditional selects. I'll wire these using the existing hooks.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1 — Upgrade Hooks to Support Filters

#### [MODIFY] [useClients.js](file:///c:/Users/Mohamed/Desktop/gabo-system-api/src/hooks/api/useClients.js)
- Add `filters` param to `useClients(filters)` → passes as `params` to axios GET.

#### [MODIFY] [useEmployees.js](file:///c:/Users/Mohamed/Desktop/gabo-system-api/src/hooks/api/useEmployees.js)
- Add `filters` param to `useEmployees(filters)` → passes as `params` to axios GET.

#### [MODIFY] [useTasks.js](file:///c:/Users/Mohamed/Desktop/gabo-system-api/src/hooks/api/useTasks.js)
- Add `filters` param to `useTasks(filters)` → passes as `params` to axios GET.

#### [MODIFY] [useTransactions.js](file:///c:/Users/Mohamed/Desktop/gabo-system-api/src/hooks/api/useTransactions.js)
- Add `filters` param to `useTransactions(filters)` → passes as `params` to axios GET.

